====================================================================
  VENDOR SECURITY BULLETIN
  Microsoft Security Advisory ADV260001
====================================================================

Published:          January 28, 2026
Severity:           Important
Affected Software:  Microsoft Office 2021, Microsoft 365 Apps
CVE:                CVE-2026-20198
CVSS Score:         7.5 (High)

VULNERABILITY DESCRIPTION:
--------------------------
A remote code execution vulnerability exists in Microsoft Word when
processing specially crafted RTF documents. An attacker who successfully
exploits this vulnerability could run arbitrary code in the context of
the current user.

EXPLOITATION:
-------------
- Attack Vector: Email attachment or malicious download
- User Interaction: Required (must open document)
- Privileges Required: None
- Exploit publicly available: No (as of advisory date)

RECOMMENDED ACTIONS:
--------------------
1. Deploy update KB5035201 via WSUS or SCCM
2. Enable Protected View for Office documents from external sources
3. Block RTF attachments at email gateway (interim mitigation)
4. Educate users on phishing awareness

AFFECTED ACS SYSTEMS:
---------------------
{{ prefix }}-WS01 — User workstation (Office 2021 installed)
{{ prefix }}-DEV-Laptop-04 — Developer workstation (Microsoft 365)

ADDITIONAL NOTES:
-----------------
This advisory was released through Microsoft's standard Patch Tuesday
cycle. The vulnerability was responsibly disclosed by a third-party
researcher and no active exploitation has been observed.

